```java
public class Race {
    static int shared = 0;

    public static void main(String[] args) throws InterruptedException {
        final int N = 100_000;

        Thread a = new Thread(() -> { for (int i = 0; i < N; i++) shared++; });   // racy.
        Thread b = new Thread(() -> { for (int i = 0; i < N; i++) shared++; });
        a.start(); b.start(); a.join(); b.join();
        System.out.println(shared == 2 * N ? "lucky" : "lost updates");       // usually lost updates.

        int[] parts = new int[2];                                              // confined: one slot each.
        Thread c = new Thread(() -> { for (int i = 0; i < N; i++) parts[0]++; });
        Thread d = new Thread(() -> { for (int i = 0; i < N; i++) parts[1]++; });
        c.start(); d.start(); c.join(); d.join();                               // join orders the reads.
        System.out.println(parts[0] + parts[1]);                                // 200000
    }
}
```

| Strategy | Use when |
|---|---|
| confinement. | each task can own its own data. |
| atomic class (AtomicInteger.incrementAndGet). | one variable, simple updates. |
| synchronized or lock. | several fields must change together. |

